<section class="card" aria-labelledby="snapshot-title">
  <div class="section-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">LIVE DIAGNOSTICS</p>
      <h2 id="snapshot-title">All sixteen flags</h2>
    </div>
    <span class="small" data-snapshot-status>Checks every 3 seconds</span>
  </div>
  <p class="small">This diagnostic snapshot evaluates with your current context. Native definition polling runs every <%= @service.configuration.refresh_interval %> seconds when connected. Other sections render again on navigation or reload.</p>
  <p class="small">
    Each row pairs a boolean and reason from one native evaluation. Rows may observe
    different revisions during a refresh. Diagnostics do not apply
    <code>enabled?</code> fallbacks or record automatic usage checks. A missing
    definition yields OFF and <code>feature_not_found</code>;
    <a href="/gates">actual gates</a> separately apply defaults and record usage.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Flag checklist</th>
          <th>Diagnostic result</th>
          <th>Native reason</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @flags.each do |flag| %>
          <tr data-flag="<%= h(flag[:key]) %>">
            <td>
              <code>
                <%= h(flag[:key]) %>
              </code>
            </td>
            <td data-state>
              <%= state_badge(flag[:enabled]) %>
            </td>
            <td data-reason>
              <%= h(flag[:reason]) %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small">SDK ready: <strong data-ready>
      <%= h(@client.ready) %>
    </strong>. A restored file snapshot can supply evaluated values while native readiness is false during a startup outage. Both are shown as reported.</p>
</section>
